---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { breadcrumbNode, pageSchema } from '../data/schema';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const updated = 'October 28, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Terms & Conditions | Goat Garage Door Service"
	description="Terms for using the Goat Garage Door Service website and for requesting residential garage door repair or installation."
	schema={pageSchema([
		breadcrumbNode([
			{ name: 'Home', path: '/' },
			{ name: 'Terms & Conditions', path: '/terms' },
		]),
	])}
>
	<PageHero
		title="Terms & Conditions"
		lead="How this website works, and what a request for service means."
		crumbs={[
			{ label: 'Home', href: '/' },
			{ label: 'Terms & Conditions' },
		]}
	/>
	<section class="section">
		<div class="container prose" style="max-width: 760px;">
			<p>Last updated {updated}.</p>
			<p>
				These terms cover {site.domain.replace('https://', '')} and a request for garage door service from {site.name}.
				We are based at {site.address.street}, {site.address.city}, {site.address.region} {site.address.postalCode}.
				Using the site means you agree to these terms. If you do not, please leave the site and call or email instead.
			</p>

			<h2>Quotes and the work</h2>
			<p>
				The form asks for a free, no-obligation estimate. Sending it, or calling, does not hire us and does not lock in a price.
				We look at the door, tell you what failed, and give you the price before the repair starts. You can decline.
			</p>
			<p>
				A price covers the work we described. If we open the door and find a different problem — a second spring, a bad cable, a section that will not take a new seal — we stop and tell you before that extra work goes ahead.
				Pages on this site describe typical jobs. They are not a quote for your door.
			</p>

			<h2>Scheduling and where we work</h2>
			<p>
				Hours are {site.hours}. Emergency calls are for a door that leaves the house open, traps the cars, or is hanging crooked.
				Planned installs and other non-urgent work are scheduled when we follow up.
			</p>
			<p>
				We serve Fishers, Indianapolis, and the surrounding towns listed on the service area pages. If a job is outside that area, we will say so before we come out.
				Arrival times are estimates. Weather, traffic, and a door that is unsafe to leave can change the order of the day.
			</p>

			<h2>At the house</h2>
			<p>Please have the following ready when we arrive:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>A clear path to the door, with cars and stored items moved off the tracks and the floor in front of the door</li>
				<li>Someone 18 or older who can approve the price</li>
				<li>Pets kept away from the work area</li>
				<li>Power to the opener, unless you have already unplugged it because it is grinding or reversing on its own</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				Springs and cables are under tension. Please leave a broken spring, a loose cable, or a crooked door alone until we get there.
				Do not wind a spring, pull the red release on a door the springs no longer balance, or keep cycling an opener that is straining.
			</p>

			<h2>Payment</h2>
			<p>
				Payment is due when the work we agreed on is finished, unless the written quote for that job says otherwise.
				The quote or invoice for the visit is the record of the price, the parts, and any warranty we offered on that job.
			</p>

			<h2>Parts and warranties</h2>
			<p>
				Any warranty on labor or on a part we install is the warranty written on the quote or invoice for that job.
				A manufacturer’s warranty, when one applies, comes from the part maker and follows that maker’s terms.
				Descriptions, photos, and service pages on this website are not a warranty.
			</p>

			<h2>The website</h2>
			<p>
				Text, photos, and the logo belong to {site.name}. You may look at them and share a link to a page.
				Please do not copy the photos, the logo, or page text for your own site or ads.
			</p>
			<p>
				We try to keep the site accurate. Service descriptions can change, and a page can be out of date.
				The site may be unavailable while it is updated or while the host has an outage.
				Links to maps, Facebook, or other sites leave our site, and those sites have their own terms.
			</p>
			<p>
				The service form is delivered through Netlify so we can read it. How we handle what you send is on the
				<a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
			</p>

			<h2>Liability</h2>
			<p>
				To the extent Indiana law allows, {site.name} is not liable for indirect or consequential damages from using this website, from a form that does not arrive, or from a delay in answering a request.
				Nothing on this page limits liability that Indiana law does not allow a service business to limit.
			</p>

			<h2>Indiana law</h2>
			<p>
				These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Indiana. Disputes about the website or a request for service are handled in the state or federal courts located in Indiana.
			</p>

			<h2>Changes</h2>
			<p>
				We can update these terms by posting a new version on this page. The date at the top is the date of the current version.
				A job already quoted keeps the terms we gave you with that quote.
			</p>

			<h2>Contact</h2>
			<p>
				Questions about these terms: call <a href={`tel:${site.phoneTel}`}>{site.phoneDisplay}</a> or email
				<a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>
